  "text" : "This model's ROC area under the curve is 0.95, nearly perfect, but most of what it\nflags is wrong.\nAUC is for comparing models.\nA coin flip is 0.5.\nYou pick a random attack and a random user, and 98.5% of the time the attack scores higher.\nNow look at this point.\nFalse positive rate 2.3%, sounds small.\nIt's 233 real users blocked just to catch 44 attacks.\nSo swap the false positive rate for precision.\nPrecision doesn't use true negatives.\nRecall goes across, precision goes up, and the same model's curve drops.\nNow the good corner is top right.\nAnd the coin flip here isn't 0.5.\nIt's.005, the attack rate.\nThis model's precision recall area under the curve is 0.56.\nIt's low looking, but over 100 times better than chance.\nWhen positives are rare, we want to compare models on the precision recall curve."
}
